A product card: a photo with a discount badge and a wishlist toggle, the name and prices, a size picker, a quantity
field and an Add to cart button. A **block** composed from [Badge](<%= page_path(:badge) %>),
[Toggle](<%= page_path(:toggle) %>), [Toggle Group](<%= page_path(:toggle_group) %>),
[Number Field](<%= page_path(:number_field) %>) and [Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>), as on the
[Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui).

<%= embed AppicaUI::Blocks::ProductCardPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
ProductCard(name: product.name, description: product.subtitle, image: product.photo_url, image_alt: product.photo_alt,
  price: product.price, original_price: product.list_price, action: cart_items_path, product_id: product.id) do
  ProductOptions(sizes: product.sizes, selected: product.default_size)
  ProductAddToCart()
end
```

- A lower `price:` than `original_price:` shows the struck-through original and a discount badge ("−20%");
  `badge:` replaces the badge text, `badge: nil` hides it.
- The heart is a Toggle (`wishlisted:` starts it pressed; `wishlist: false` drops it).
- `ProductOptions` renders the size ToggleGroup (sizes past `compact:` hide on small screens) and a quantity
  NumberField (1 to `max:`).
- With `action:` the card is a `<form>`: Add to cart posts `product_id`, `size` and `quantity`.

```ruby
# app/controllers/cart_items_controller.rb
def create
  Current.cart.items.create!(product_id: params[:product_id], size: params[:size], quantity: params[:quantity])
  redirect_to cart_path
end
```

## Localization

`product_card.locales.yml` holds the wishlist, size, quantity and button labels; the prices and badge use the locale's
number format. Switch the **Locale** display option to try it.

